{
  "finding_summary": "The discrepancy between Stage 3 (0.8922) and Stage 7 pre-drift (0.3800-0.4400 per window, 0.5599 pooled) is a pure class-support artifact of zero-division macro-averaging over small windows. In any small window of 900 evaluation rows, only 7 to 11 of the 25 classes are present. Because the classifier achieves 99.8% to 100.0% Macro-F1 on all present active classes, the 25-class Macro-F1 is mathematically bounded by (active_classes / 25). When pooling all pre-drift windows (w0-w5), 14 classes appear and Macro-F1 rises to 0.5599 (100% active F1). In Stage 3, the test set has 315,004 rows across all 5 days where all 25 classes are present, yielding 0.8922.",
